    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0386" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00–1374</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Russell to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-10T18:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1916, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign Office has just advised me of a cable received from Dominican Legation,
                    Port au Prince, dated eighth, as follows: Armed manifestation against Americans,
                    several important arrests, grave events awaited. Dominican Minister left.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
